{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRsdCPLJczBv4UtbLNua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I raised `CARRIER_TIMEOUT_MS` in `lib/carrier.js:4` from `10_000` to `30_000`. Nothing else in the repo refers to the old value, and all 30 tests pass. I haven't committed the change.\n\nThis should stop the duplicate labels in the case you described, where the carrier takes 10–20 seconds. It doesn't remove the underlying problem. `callCarrier` still retries up to 5 times (`MAX_ATTEMPTS` in `lib/retry.js`) on any failure, timeouts included. If the carrier ever takes longer than 30 seconds, we'd give up, retry, and buy a second label again, up to five times over.\n\nTo close that gap, you could:\n- **Idempotency key:** send one per label request, if the carrier supports it, so a retry returns the original label.\n- **Skip retries for label issuance:** don't retry on a timeout for that operation. Retry only on errors where the carrier clearly didn't act.\n- **Check before retrying:** after a timeout, look up whether a label already exists before sending another request.\n\nI haven't made any of these changes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1089,"cache_read_input_tokens":23252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1089,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":366,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be961d52-7bc1-4514-8d44-8aabbc5afbdf","uuid":"a4005559-7fa9-4b80-9afb-f115a6e9752d","timestamp":"2026-11-26T16:42:32.060Z","request_id":"req_011ChRsdCFA2o9yCLK7YiyPR"}
